@startuml Documented Architecture - Contract-Aware Webhook Flow
!theme plain
title <font size=24 color="#2E7D32"><b>DOCUMENTED: Contract-Aware Webhook Flow</b></font>\n<font size=14 color="#558B2F">From 05-02-webhooks-with-smart-contracts.md</font>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000

skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor<<stripe>> #E3F2FD
    BackgroundColor<<contract>> #C8E6C9
    BackgroundColor<<order>> #FFF3E0
    BackgroundColor<<db>> #F3E5F5
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFACD
    BorderColor #FFA000
    FontColor #000000
}

box "External" #ECEFF1
    participant "Stripe" as Stripe <<stripe>>
end box

box "Webhook Layer" #E8F5E9
    participant "WebhookController" as WC
    participant "WebhookProcessingService" as WPS
end box

box "Contract Layer (Component)" #C8E6C9
    participant "ContractRepository" as CR <<contract>>
    participant "PaymentContract" as PC <<contract>>
end box

box "Order Layer" #FFF3E0
    participant "OrderRepository" as OR <<order>>
    participant "Order" as O <<order>>
end box

box "Database" #F3E5F5
    database "osc_payment_contract" as DBContract <<db>>
    database "osc_payment_transaction" as DBTrans <<db>>
    database "oxorder" as DBOrder <<db>>
end box

== Documented Flow (Smart-Contract Pattern) ==

Stripe -> WC : POST /webhook/stripe\nEvent: payment_intent.succeeded
activate WC #90CAF9

WC -> WC : Verify signature
WC -> WPS : processEvent(event)
activate WPS #A5D6A7

note right of WPS #C8E6C9
  **STEP 1: Find Contract**
  Contract is the central entity!
end note

WPS -> CR : findByProviderOrderId("pi_xxx")
activate CR #81C784
CR -> DBContract : SELECT * FROM osc_payment_contract\nWHERE OXPROVIDERORDERID = 'pi_xxx'
DBContract --> CR : contract_data
CR --> WPS : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

note right of WPS #FFFDE7
  **STEP 2: Validate State**
  Only process COMMITTED contracts!
end note

WPS -> PC : getState()
PC --> WPS : COMMITTED

alt Contract State == FULFILLED
    WPS --> WC : Already processed (idempotent)
else Contract State == COMMITTED
    note right of WPS #C8E6C9
      **STEP 3: Fulfill Contract**
      Transition: COMMITTED -> FULFILLED
    end note

    WPS -> PC : fulfill()
    PC --> WPS : state = FULFILLED

    WPS -> CR : save(contract)
    CR -> DBContract : UPDATE state = 'FULFILLED'\nOXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()

    note right of WPS #FFF3E0
      **STEP 4: Update Order**
      Order is updated THROUGH contract
    end note

    WPS -> OR : find(contract.getOrderId())
    OR -> DBOrder : SELECT * FROM oxorder
    DBOrder --> OR : order_data
    OR --> WPS : Order

    WPS -> O : markOrderPaid()
    WPS -> O : setState('OK')

    WPS -> OR : save(order)
    OR -> DBOrder : UPDATE OXPAID, OXTRANSSTATUS

    note right of WPS #E3F2FD
      **STEP 5: Emit Event**
      Event-driven architecture!
    end note

    WPS -> WPS : dispatch(ContractFulfilledEvent)
end

WPS --> WC : processed
deactivate WPS

WC --> Stripe : 200 OK
deactivate WC

legend right
  |= Color |= Layer |= Responsibility |
  | <#C8E6C9> | Contract | Central entity, state machine |
  | <#FFF3E0> | Order | Updated through contract |
  | <#E3F2FD> | Event System | Event-driven architecture |
endlegend

footer <font color="#2E7D32"><b>This is how it SHOULD work according to documentation</b></font>

@enduml
